# Research/scratch work.
#
# The write-ups and the probe sources are kept - they are our own analysis and code.
# What those probes HARVESTED is not: scraped BOOTH catalog JSON, text extracted from
# purchased PDFs, and downloaded product images are all third-party content.
# The scripts that produce them are here, so anyone can regenerate the data locally.
#
# ONE EXCEPTION is committed: assets/booth-categories.json, BOOTH's category table.
# It is a classification structure, not a seller's work - short functional names whose
# purpose is interoperability, and we already store the same strings in every item JSON.
# We bundle it so that a thousand users do not each fetch the same static table from
# BOOTH; the rule here exists to reduce their load, and fetching it per-user would
# increase it. Regenerate with experiments/CategoryFetch (one request). See NOTICE.
research/*
!research/.gitignore
!research/*.md
!research/*.ps1
!research/PdfProbe
research/PdfProbe/*
!research/PdfProbe/*.cs
!research/PdfProbe/*.csproj

# Claude Code local settings. The project skills and path-scoped rules are shared (work procedures and rules only - no friend data)
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/settings.json
